//
// Normative rule Zicfiss_vu_senvcfg_sse (src/priv/cfi.adoc):
//   Otherwise, if in VU-mode and senvcfg[sse] is 0, a virtual-instruction exception is raised.
//
// Context:
//   menvcfg.SSE=1. With V=1 and henvcfg.SSE=0, senvcfg.SSE is read-only zero (henvcfg_sse_op), so
//     VU-mode also raises virtual-instruction when HS-mode set senvcfg.SSE but henvcfg.SSE=0.
//
// Clarifications:
//   https://github.com/riscv/riscv-isa-manual/issues/2424: "When henvcfg.sse is 0 and V is 1,
//     senvcfg.sse is read only zero. A read only zero CSR field cannot be written to and returns 0
//     on read by both hardware and software" (ved-rivos). So VU-mode with henvcfg.SSE=0 sees
//     senvcfg.SSE=0 whatever HS-mode wrote.
//
// Test plan:
//   1. menvcfg.SSE=1, henvcfg.SSE=1, senvcfg.SSE=0: every CSR form on ssp in VU-mode raises
//     virtual-instruction (xtval 0 or the instruction bits); ssp is unchanged.
//   2. U-mode (V=0) with the same enables raises illegal-instruction instead (the U bullet).
//   3. senvcfg.SSE=1: VU-mode reads and writes succeed.
//   4. senvcfg.SSE=1 but henvcfg.SSE=0: VU-mode raises virtual-instruction (senvcfg.SSE reads zero
//     when V=1).
//
// Approximate dynamic instruction count: 3117
//

